-- two evidence slots of one call that EACH nest get their own evidence,
-- and not each other's (`docs/design/static-dispatch-spike.md` §7.2, §8.2,
-- A.68).
--
-- The site list of one instruction is FLAT and the evidence it describes is
-- a TREE: a slot answered by a function that takes evidence of its own
-- consumes the slots that follow it. §7.2 numbers the slots with a running
-- cursor, which is allocation order, and allocation is breadth-first — one
-- instantiation numbers every slot of its own `where` clause before any of
-- them is discharged. With one nesting chain that is still pre-order by
-- accident; with TWO slots that each nest it is not, and the walk read
-- `a`'s children as `b`'s.
--
-- `pair [ [ 1 ] ] [ [ 1 ] ] [ [ 2 ] ] [ [ 2 ] ]` is the whole of it. The
-- emitted call handed `a` a `List$eq` nested FOUR deep and handed `b` a
-- bare `===`, which on two distinct arrays is `false` — so line 1 printed
-- `False` where the language says `True`, and lines 4 and 6 crashed
-- `List.eq` on a number with `TypeError: Cannot read properties of
-- undefined`, after a build that exited 0.
--
-- Every line here needs BOTH slots' evidence to be its own. Lines 2 and 3
-- differ in exactly one slot, so a program that wired one slot's evidence
-- into the other still has to disagree with one of them; line 4 gives the
-- two slots different SHAPES, `List (List Int)` against `List (Maybe Int)`,
-- so swapping them is a type the other could not survive; line 6 makes
-- slot `b` a tuple, whose evidence rides on the target's own `part` tree
-- (§7.1) rather than on the site list, and slot `a`'s element evidence has
-- to land between the two all the same. The last three are the same shape
-- through `compare` and `<`, where the nesting is a derived `Maybe$compare`
-- taking the inner `Maybe`'s comparator rather than a `foreign` List.
import Maybe exposing (Maybe)
import Node exposing (Program)


pub pair : a, a, b, b -> Bool
    where
        a.eq : a, a -> Bool
        , b.eq : b, b -> Bool
pair x1 x2 y1 y2 =
    x1 == x2 && y1 == y2


pub less : a, a, b, b -> Bool
    where
        a.compare : a, a -> Order
        , b.compare : b, b -> Order
less x1 x2 y1 y2 =
    x1 < x2 && y1 < y2


show : Bool -> String
show b =
    if b then
        "True"

    else
        "False"


main : Program
main =
    Node.printLines
        [ show (pair [ [ 1 ] ] [ [ 1 ] ] [ [ 2 ] ] [ [ 2 ] ])
        , show (pair [ [ 1 ] ] [ [ 9 ] ] [ [ 2 ] ] [ [ 2 ] ])
        , show (pair [ [ 1 ] ] [ [ 1 ] ] [ [ 2 ] ] [ [ 9 ] ])
        , show (pair [ [ 1, 2 ] ] [ [ 1, 2 ] ] [ Just 3 ] [ Just 3 ])
        , show (pair [ [ 1, 2 ] ] [ [ 1, 2 ] ] [ Just 3 ] [ Just 4 ])
        , show (pair [ 1 ] [ 1 ] ( [ [ 2 ] ], [ [ 3 ] ] ) ( [ [ 2 ] ], [ [ 3 ] ] ))
        , show (pair [ 1 ] [ 1 ] ( [ [ 2 ] ], [ [ 3 ] ] ) ( [ [ 2 ] ], [ [ 9 ] ] ))
        , show (less (Just (Just 1)) (Just (Just 2)) (Just (Just 3)) (Just (Just 4)))
        , show (less (Just (Just 1)) (Just (Just 2)) (Just (Just 5)) (Just (Just 4)))
        , show (less (Just (Just 2)) (Just (Just 2)) (Just (Just 3)) (Just (Just 4)))
        ]
